   "source": [
    "# 📖 Prompts and Tokens: The Building Blocks of LLM Interactions\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🎯 Learning Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "By the end of this notebook, you will:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Understand** what tokens are and how tokenization works\n",
    "2. **Master** few-shot learning and in-context learning\n",
    "3. **Apply** prompt engineering techniques to get better outputs\n",
    "4. **Handle** token limits and context windows\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## ⏱️ Time Estimate\n",
    "\n",
    "**~25 minutes**\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 📦 Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q openai tiktoken\n",
    "import os\n",
    "if \"OPENAI_API_KEY\" not in os.environ:\n",
    "    import getpass\n",
    "    os.environ[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"] = getpass.getpass(\"Enter OpenAI API Key: \")\n",
    "\n",
    "from openai import OpenAI\n",
    "client = OpenAI()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🧠 Theory: Understanding Tokens\n",
    "\n",
    "### What Are Tokens?\n",
    "\n",
    "Tokens are the **basic units** an LLM processes. They're NOT exactly words - they're subword units:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Text | Tokenization Example |\n",
    "|------|----------------------|\n",
    "| \"hello\" | [\"hello\"] |\n",
    "| \"unhappiness\" | [\"un\", \"happ\", \"iness\"] |\n",
    "| \"LLM\" | [\"LLM\"] |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why Tokens Matter\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│                  TOKEN ECONOMICS                    │\n",
    "├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n",
    "│  • API pricing is based on total tokens (in + out)  │\n",
    "│  • Context window = max tokens you can send         │\n",
    "│  • Less tokens = faster + cheaper                    │\n",
    "└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import tiktoken\n",
    "\n",
    "# Let's see exactly how text gets tokenized\n",
    "enc = tiktoken.get_encoding(\"cl100k_base\")  # OpenAI's encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "texts = [\n",
    "    \"hello world\",\n",
    "    \"unhappiness\",\n",
    "    \"Large Language Models are amazing!\",\n",
    "    \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\",\n",
    "    \"🥶 emoji test 123!\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🔢 Tokenization Examples\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
    "for text in texts:\n",
    "    tokens = enc.encode(text)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nText: \\\"{text}\\\\"\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Tokens: {tokens}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Token count: {len(tokens)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Key Insight: Token Efficiency\n",
    "\n",
    "| Text Type | Approx Tokens |\n",
    "|-----------|---------------|\n",
    "| 1 English word | ~1-2 tokens |\n",
    "| 1 Chinese character | ~1 token |\n",
    "| 1 emoji | ~2 tokens |\n",
    "| 1 code character | ~1-4 tokens |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pro tip**: Shorter prompts cost less and run faster!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 💬 System/User Roles & Prompt Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's master the art of crafting effective prompts:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example 1: Basic prompting (no system context)\n",
    "response1 = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Summarize this: Python is a great programming language.\"}],\n",
    "    max_tokens=50\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"❌ BAD PROMPT (no context):\")\n",
    "print(response1.choices[0].message.content)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example 2: Better prompting with system context\n",
    "response2 = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "    messages=[\n",
    "        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a Python expert. Give concise, technical answers.\"},\n",
    "        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Summarize this: Python is a great programming language.\"}\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    max_tokens=50\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"\\n✅ GOOD PROMPT (with system context):\")\n",
    "print(response2.choices[0].message.content)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🎓 Few-Shot Learning: Teaching by Example\n",
    "\n",
    "Few-shot learning means giving the model EXAMPLES of what you want:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# WITHOUT few-shot (0-shot)\n",
    "response_zs = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "    messages=[\n",
    "        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Convert this to uppercase: hello world\"}\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    max_tokens=30\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"0-SHOT (no examples):\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Input: 'hello world' → Output: {response_zs.choices[0].message.content}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# WITH few-shot (3-shot)\n",
    "response_fs = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "    messages=[\n",
    "        {\"role\": \"user\", \n",
    "         \"content\": \"\"\"Convert to uppercase:\n",
    "input: hello world\n",
    "output: HELLO WORLD\n",
    "input: python is fun\n",
    "output: PYTHON IS FUN\n",
    "input: agents are great\n",
    "output: \"\"\"}\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    max_tokens=30\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"\\n3-SHOT (with examples):\n",
    "  Input: 'hello world' → HELLO WORLD\n",
    "  Input: 'python is fun' → PYTHON IS FUN\n",
    "  Input: 'agents are great' → Output:\" + response_fs.choices[0].message.content)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Few-Shot Best Practices\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│               FEW-SHOT FORMULA                     │\n",
    "├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n",
    "│  Pattern: [input] → [output] repeated 2-5 times     │\n",
    "│                                                     │\n",
    "│  Tips:                                                 │\n",
    "│  • Use 2-5 examples for complex tasks                │\n",
    "│  • Keep examples diverse                             │\n",
    "│  • Use exact same format                           │\n",
    "│  • Examples count toward token limit!              │\n",
    "└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🔄 Chain of Thought (CoT) Prompting\n",
    "\n",
    "Chain of Thought helps the model reason through complex problems:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# WITHOUT Chain of Thought\n",
    "response_no_cot = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"If I have 5 apples and give 2 to Alice and 2 to Bob, how many do I have left?\"}],\n",
    "    max_tokens=30\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"WITHOUT CoT:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  {response_no_cot.choices[0].message.content}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# WITH Chain of Thought (adding \"think step by step\")\n",
    "response_cot = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"If I have 5 apples and give 2 to Alice and 2 to Bob, how many do I have left? Think step by step.\"}],\n",
    "    max_tokens=100\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"\\nWITH Chain of Thought:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  {response_cot.choices[0].message.content}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 📏 Handling Context Windows & Token Limits\n",
    "\n",
    "Every model has a maximum context window:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate token usage\n",
    "def count_tokens(text, encoding=\"cl100k_base\"):\n",
    "    enc = tiktoken.get_encoding(encoding)\n",
    "    return len(enc.encode(text))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check context window for different models\n",
    "models_info = [\n",
    "    (\"gpt-4o-mini\", 128000),\n",
    "    (\"gpt-4o\", 128000),\n",
    "    (\"gpt-4\", 8192),\n",
    "    (\"gpt-3.5-turbo\", 16385),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"📊 Model Context Windows\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 40)\n",
    "for model, window in models_info:\n",
    "    print(f\"{model}: {window:,} tokens max\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check a sample prompt size\n",
    "sample_prompt = \"\"\"\n",
    "You are a helpful assistant. Your task is to analyze the following code and provide feedback.\n",
    "Consider: code quality, potential bugs, performance issues, and security concerns.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSample prompt: {count_tokens(sample_prompt)} tokens\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### What Happens When You Exceed the Limit?\n",
    "\n",
    "| Issue | Solution |\n",
    "|-------|----------|\n",
    "**| Exceed context window | Truncation or summarize old messages |\n",
    "**| Very long conversations | Use summarization or start fresh |\n",
    "**| Important info lost | Put key info at start AND end |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## ⚠️ Common Prompting Mistakes\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's see what NOT to do:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# MISTAKE 1: Ambiguous instructions\n",
    "response = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Make it shorter\"}],\n",
    "    max_tokens=50\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"⚠️ MISTAKE 1: Ambiguous\")\n",
    "print(f\"  'Make it shorter' → {response.choices[0].message.content}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  ❓ Shorter WHAT? In what way?\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# MISTAKE 2: Not specifying format\n",
    "response = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"List the planets\"}],\n",
    "    max_tokens=50\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"\\n⚠️ MISTAKE 2: No format specified\")\n",
    "print(f\"  'List the planets' → {response.choices[0].message.content}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  ❓ Is this a sentence? List? Table?\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# CORRECT: Specific with format\n",
    "response = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"List the 8 planets in our solar system. Format: bullet points, one per line.\"}],\n",
    "    max_tokens=100\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"\\n✅ CORRECT: Specific + format\")\n",
    "print(f\"  {response.choices[0].message.content}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
